This confirms the intent: commit `a9c1ded` aimed to also lock food level for players in lobby/spectator areas, but in doing so dropped the `inArena(p)` guard for the "arena is running" branch — meaning players *not* in the arena (e.g., a player who just left, or any player while an arena instance is running elsewhere) would have their food level incorrectly locked. The bug-fixing commit `5058c47` restores that missing guard.

## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: a9c1ded76ed1fc157add8ef73565bd6112967bf1

## Reasoning

**(1) Investigation:** I traced the history of the `onFoodLevelChange` method in `ArenaListener.java` using `git log -p --follow` on that file, then located the exact point where the pre-fix code (`if (lockFoodLevel) { event.setCancelled(true); }` inside `if (arena.isRunning())`) was introduced, by finding which commit's diff added that `isRunning()`/`lockFoodLevel` structure without an `inArena` check.

**(2) Specific change:** Commit `a9c1ded76ed1fc157add8ef73565bd6112967bf1` ("Food levels no longer deplete for players in the lobby and spectator area" per changelog.md) rewrote `onFoodLevelChange`. The original code was:
```java
if (!arena.isRunning()) return;
if (!(event.getEntity() instanceof Player) || !arena.inArena((Player) event.getEntity())) return;
if (lockFoodLevel) event.setCancelled(true);
```
It was replaced with:
```java
if (!(event.getEntity() instanceof Player)) return;
Player p = (Player) event.getEntity();
if (arena.isRunning()) {
    if (lockFoodLevel) { event.setCancelled(true); }
} else {
    if (arena.inLobby(p) || arena.inSpec(p)) { event.setCancelled(true); }
}
```
While adding the lobby/spectator handling (the else branch), the author dropped the `arena.inArena(p)` check from the `isRunning()` branch, so any player's food-level change would be cancelled whenever the arena was running — even if that player was not actually in the arena.

**(3) Evidence:** 
- `git log a9c1ded..5058c47 -- ArenaListener.java` shows only `a9c1ded`, `cc78657`, and `7004571` touched the file afterward, and I verified `cc78657`/`7004571` modified unrelated hunks (e.g., `monsterInfight` logic), not this method.
- The fix commit `5058c47` simply re-adds the missing condition: `if (arena.inArena(p) && lockFoodLevel)`, which is exactly the guard removed in `a9c1ded`.
- The changelog entry added in `a9c1ded` confirms this was an intentional feature change (locking food for lobby/spec players) that inadvertently broke the existing arena-membership check.

I'm confident in this attribution — the diff shows a direct causal removal-then-restoration of the same guard clause with no intervening modifications to that code path.

